WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.037
An Abrams:

00:00:01.047 --> 00:00:02.862
about 64 tonnes.

00:00:02.872 --> 00:00:04.555
Your car presses harder.

00:00:04.565 --> 00:00:05.800
Lift the turret.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:06.788
The engine:

00:00:06.798 --> 00:00:10.537
a gas turbine, up to 1,500 horsepower.

00:00:10.547 --> 00:00:12.963
It can run on jet fuel, diesel

00:00:12.973 --> 00:00:13.959
or petrol.

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:15.801
Yet a car presses on the ground

00:00:15.811 --> 00:00:17.612
about twice as hard.

00:00:17.622 --> 00:00:19.713
That's why it's much less likely than

00:00:19.723 --> 00:00:21.686
a car to get stuck in mud.

00:00:21.696 --> 00:00:23.551
The secret is underneath:

00:00:23.561 --> 00:00:25.501
the tracks spread all that weight over

00:00:25.511 --> 00:00:27.011
a huge footprint.
